[Event "Petroff: 3.Nxe5"]

{The Petroff (2...Nf6) counterattacks e4 instead of defending e5.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e5 {Classical. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
2. Nf3 {Attacks e5. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
2... Nf6 {[%cal Gf6e4] The Petroff. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
3. Nxe5 {Takes. The knight on e5 eyes the pawn on d7 and the pawn on f7.}
3... d6 {First kick the knight. 3...Nxe4? 4.Qe2 is a known trap.}
4. Nf3 {Retreats. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
 (4. Nc4 {A rarer retreat. The knight on c4 eyes the pawn on d6 and controls e5.}
4... Nxe4 {Takes. The knight on e4 eyes the pawn on d2 and the pawn on f2.}
5. Qe2 {Pins along the e-file. The queen on e2 eyes the knight on e4.}
5... Qe7 {Breaks the pin and offers a queen trade.}
)
4... Nxe4 {Now takes e4. The knight on e4 eyes the pawn on d2 and the pawn on f2.}
5. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
 (5. Nc3 {Trades knights. The knight on c3 eyes the knight on e4 and controls d5.}
5... Nxc3 {Takes. The knight on c3 eyes the pawn on a2 and the queen on d1 and controls d5 and e4.}
6. dxc3 {Recaptures, opening lines. The pawn on c3 controls d4.}
6... Be7 {Develops.}
7. Be3 {Develops. The bishop on e3 eyes the pawn on a7 and controls d4.}
7... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
8. Qd2 {Prepares O-O-O. The queen on d2 eyes the pawn on d6 and controls d4 and d5.}
8... Be6 {Develops. The bishop on e6 eyes the pawn on a2 and controls d5.}
)
5... d5 {Supports the knight.}
6. Bd3 {Develops. The bishop on d3 eyes the knight on e4.}
6... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on d4 and controls e5.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... Be7 {Develops.}
8. c4 {Hits d5. The pawn on c4 eyes the pawn on d5.}
8... Nb4 {Hits the bishop. The knight on b4 eyes the bishop on d3 and the pawn on a2.}
9. Be2 {Retreats.}
9... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.} *

[Event "Petroff: 3.d4"]

{White can also open with 3.d4.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e5 {Classical. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
2. Nf3 {Attacks e5. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
2... Nf6 {Petroff. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
3. d4 {Opens. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on e5.}
3... Nxe4 {Counterattacks. The knight on e4 eyes the pawn on f2.}
 (3... exd4 {Opens the centre.}
4. e5 {Kicks the knight. The pawn on e5 eyes the knight on f6.}
4... Ne4 {Central post. The knight on e4 eyes the pawn on f2.}
5. Qxd4 {Regains the pawn. The queen on d4 eyes the pawn on a7 and the pawn on d7 and controls d5.}
5... d5 {Supports the knight.}
)
4. Bd3 {Develops. The bishop on d3 eyes the knight on e4.}
4... d5 {Supports.}
5. Nxe5 {Takes. The knight on e5 eyes the pawn on f7.}
5... Nd7 {Challenges. The knight on d7 eyes the knight on e5.}
6. Nxd7 {Trades. The knight on d7 eyes the bishop on f8 and controls e5.}
6... Bxd7 {Recaptures.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... Bd6 {Develops. The bishop on d6 eyes the pawn on h2 and controls e5.} *
